 2. Exclusive: Primordial powers up 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 A drone follows a Primordial Labs employee during a demo in Virginia. Photo: Colin Demarest/Axios

 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Primordial Labs raised $18 million in equity and will use the money to deepen its engineering, product and growth teams as well as speed deployment of Anura, its human-machine interface, CEO Lee Ritholtz told me.

 Why it matters: Success on the battlefield is increasingly defined by how smoothly troops interact with and operate alongside robotics , whether that's on land, in the sea or in the air.

 Follow the money: The Series A financing, announced this morning, was led by Ballistic Ventures.

 Squadra Ventures and Lockheed Martin Ventures participated. How it works: Anura turns plain-English voice commands into action. So far, it's aboard more than a dozen crewed and uncrewed systems.

 Users can execute simple adjustments, like climbing a small drone to a higher altitude, or complex tasks, like repositioning an armored vehicle's sensors to a new point of interest. Neither requires memorized lines or special syntax. That reduces mental burden, especially on the front line. What they're saying: "Warfare has changed. The battlefield has changed . Systems can't be stagnant," Ritholtz said.

 "We want soldiers that can move between platforms," he added, "and from anywhere in a human-machine-integrated formation, they should be able to interact with that machine without having to go through a training course." Flashback: Primordial and General Dynamics Land Systems, maker of the Abrams and Stryker, in October announced a "master teaming agreement."

 What's next: The startup is eyeing office space in Detroit and Huntsville, Alabama, as well as an "expansion" overseas, according to Ritholtz.

 "A lot of these platforms are used internationally," he said. "Apache is used around the world. Abrams? Used around the world, like in Taiwan." Go deeper: Primordial Labs is translating human voices into drone commands 

 
 
