A MESSAGE FROM NORTHROP GRUMMAN

 
 Innovative defense tech is fueling high-skill jobs nationwide 
 &nbsp; 
 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 The future of defense won’t be decided by ideas alone, but by who can build them at scale. Northrop Grumman turns advanced concepts into real systems and high-skill jobs, linking factory floors and supplier networks to the nation’s security and economic strength.


 Dive deeper. 


 
 &nbsp; 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 
 4. Exclusive: Intalus expansion plans 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 Illustration: Sarah Grillo/Axios

 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Intalus, an advanced materials company , is expanding its production footprint with financing from Rochefort, a firm licensed under the Small Business Administration and the Pentagon's Office of Strategic Capital .

 Why it matters: "We're turning myths about American manufacturing on their head," Steve Place, the company's head of corporate strategy, told me.

 "We can still make world-class manufacturing technology in this country." Zoom in: The financing, which the company declined to put a specific number on, will fund facilities and machines that:

 Use heat and pressure to close internal voids and reduce defects in metal parts; Infuse components with ceramic-metal material that improves heat, wear and corrosion resistance. Zoom out: These processes, dubbed HIP+ and TPI, are relevant for turbines and reactors in submarines , aerospace engineering, and munitions and energetics production.

 "What the future looks like is net-new capabilities," Place said. "We regularly talk to companies building the future that are limited by current manufacturing technology." Follow the money: Intalus has raised more than $30 million thus far. Backers include Scout Ventures and Lockheed Martin Ventures.

 Semafor reported its $11 million seed. Tectonic reported an additional $20 million raise. What's next: The company has plans for six "major locations across the country," chief executive and co-founder Gene Skiba told me.

 "We need to scale and think differently," he said. "How do we actually provide improved capabilities to the engineers, so we can make better products?" Go deeper: Why American reindustrialization feels like "jazz and rock and roll" 

 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 
 5. Quick hits 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 Illustration: Lindsey Bailey/Axios

 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 🤖 Machina was selected to develop and qualify a robo-crafted, metal-based airframe for LUCAS drones and plans to deploy two expeditionary factories to support production.

 Why it matters: "This program brings our 'build anything, anywhere' mission to life," CEO Ed Mehr said in a statement, and brings "production capacity closer to the point of need." 💭 My thought bubble: Machina early this year raised $124 million and eyed the reinvigoration of "a different blue collar." More on that, here . ‼️ Nvidia CEO Jensen Huang admitted to having a romantic relationship with a suspected Chinese spy, and U.S. House committee chairmen have summoned him to brief lawmakers behind closed doors.

 Why it matters: The potential geopolitical, technological and financial consequences are astounding. 💭 My thought bubble: My colleague Madison Mills has more here and here . Another colleague, Donica Phifer, has additional reporting here . 📈 CesiumAstro raised $730 million. The round, led by Janus Henderson, brings the company's total capital announced this year to more than $1.2 billion. It's now valued north of $4.5 billion.

 Why it matters: Whopping numbers . No other way to put it. 💭 My thought bubble: CesiumAstro has made some interesting acquisitions, including Jariet Technologies, 1Aardvark and Vidrovr. ⚓ France's Naval Group unveiled a warship concept dubbed SCX 26, described in videos as "collaborative-combat ready," "drone-centric," "heavily armed" and "hyperconnected."

 Why it matters: "The return of high-intensity conflict and the emergence of hybrid naval warfare" requires a "new vision," the company said on X . 💭 My thought bubble: Is Euronaval worth attending? Reply here and let me know! 
 
