 6. Check this out 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 Kim Jong-un speaks at a recent drone show in North Korea. Screenshot: Korea Central TV/via KCNA

 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Looks familiar, huh?

 The big picture: North Korea recently put on the Unmanned Aeronautical Technology Development-2026 exhibition. 

 It featured plenty of drones big and small — including Global Hawk and Reaper lookalikes , a previously unseen uncrewed combat air vehicle, and quadcopters. Zoom in: State media, citing leader Kim Jong-un, said seizing "absolute superiority in the drone technology is an indispensable option in the light of the ever-changing patterns of modern warfare."

